{"obsah":"<p>The second day camp started with a rainy day and temperatures below 20°C. Surprisingly, that didn't put off many participants, and combined with the growing interest in our camps, 27 kids came along plus a few from our club. We originally didn't want to exceed the rider limit we'd set, but the kids were disciplined and loved the bikes, so our main carers and coaches could handle it. Unfortunately we had to turn away further substitutes – hopefully see you next year.</p>\n\n<p>We covered everything from the pump track, berms and obstacles to jumps for the bravest. On Thursday there was also Trial training for everyone who owns a Trial bike. Those who don't still had the chance to try the basics during one of the sessions. The final pump track race was dramatic until the end and a nice full stop to the whole camp, where you could see improvement in most riders. Every day there were also rides around the area to build fitness (although that's not our priority, unlike technique).</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F08%2F362265089_6840991875919952_4624531086180114977_n.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F08%2F362265089_6840991875919952_4624531086180114977_n.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-237955\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F08%2F363909685_6840994599253013_8657606962626275167_n.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F08%2F363909685_6840994599253013_8657606962626275167_n.webp?alt=medi